From 063b98060442a530c620e511136ec5b7530cdebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(permissions): port the commands of LuckPerms 5.5.71

The operators of the live server read and change the permissions with
the commands of LuckPerms, in game and over RCON, and Golem has no
command for them, so a change of the permissions would need an edit of
the store by hand.

The module command of golem-permissions ports /luckperms with its
aliases /lp, /perm, /perms, /permission and /permissions: user and
group with info, permission info, set, unset, check and clear, parent
info, set, add, remove and clear and clear, setweight and listmembers
of a group, and creategroup, deletegroup and listgroups. It keeps the
names, the convenience aliases, the nodes under luckperms. and the
English texts of LuckPerms as plain text, and says what Golem does not
hold, such as a context, meta, an expiry, a track or the web editor.

A command edits a Config, the public form of the configuration, and
loads it with Permissions::from_config, so a change that breaks a rule
of the format, such as a cycle of inheritance, changes nothing. It
answers the entries it changed for the store and the permissions to
install, and names no store and no runtime, so the crate keeps its
license and its callers. The group admin of the seed grants
luckperms.*, since it stands for the operators, who held the commands
of LuckPerms through commands-allow-op on the live server.

