+   "source": [
+    "## Who may run the commands of LuckPerms\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A sender may run a command when they hold its node of LuckPerms 5.5.71, such as\n",
+    "`luckperms.user.permission.set`, by the rules of the check of a sender. Sam holds none of them, so\n",
+    "`/lp` alone tells them so, and any other command answers the version and no command of the list.\n",
+    "Once the console put Sam into the group admin, which grants `luckperms.*`, Sam may run them, and a\n",
+    "command block at level 2 may run them as every source at that level holds every node, while a\n",
+    "source below it may not. Every alias of LuckPerms runs the same command and names itself in the\n",
+    "usage."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "06c000004",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "AS_SAM = {\"uuid\": SAM, \"name\": \"Sam\", \"level\": 4}\n",
+    "refused = lp([\"\", \"user Alex info\", \"listgroups\"], sender=AS_SAM)\n",
+    "for outcome in refused:\n",
+    "    print(\"/lp %-16s %s\" % (outcome[\"arguments\"], \" / \".join(outcome[\"lines\"])))\n",
+    "assert refused[0][\"lines\"] == [RUNNING, \"[LP] You do not have permission to use any sub commands.\"], refused[0]\n",
+    "assert refused[1][\"lines\"] == refused[2][\"lines\"] == [RUNNING], refused[1:]\n",
+    "with_sam = SEED.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") + '\\n[players.%s]\\ngroups = [\"admin\"]\\n' % SAM\n",
+    "granted = lp([\"user Alex info\", \"listgroups\"], sender=AS_SAM, config=with_sam)\n",
+    "assert granted[0][\"lines\"][0] == \"[LP] > User Info: Alex\" and granted[1][\"lines\"][1] == \"[LP] Groups: (name, weight, tracks)\"\n",
+    "block = lp([\"group default permission set essentials.fly\"], sender={\"name\": \"@\", \"level\": 2})\n",
+    "assert block[0][\"lines\"] == [\"[LP] Set essentials.fly to true for default in context global.\"], block\n",
+    "low = lp([\"listgroups\"], sender={\"name\": \"Server\", \"level\": 1})\n",
+    "assert low[0][\"lines\"] == [RUNNING], low\n",
+    "for alias in [\"luckperms\", \"perm\", \"perms\", \"permission\", \"permissions\"]:\n",
+    "    usage = lp([\"help\"], label=alias)[0][\"lines\"]\n",
+    "    assert usage[1] == \"> /%s user <user>\" % alias, usage\n",
+    "print(\"Sam is refused, an admin, a command block at level 2 and every alias run the commands\")"
